  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Explore Star Groups\r\n\r\nThe warm-up compared the Sun with all stars and with stars less than 10 light years away. This program creates a different subgroup based on star color.\r\n\r\n### Step 1: Predict and Run\r\n\r\nReview the code.\r\n\r\n- What do you think the program will calculate?\r\n- Run the program and examine the output.\r\n\r\n### Step 2: Ask AI Tutor\r\n\r\nAsk AI Tutor to explain how `groupby()`, `mean()`, and `loc[]` work together in this program.\r\n\r\n### Step 3: Modify the Code\r\n\r\nThe Sun’s color is Yellow and its mass is `1`.\r\n\r\nAsk AI Tutor to help you modify the code so it calculates and prints the average mass of Yellow stars. Run the modified program.\r\n\r\nIs the average mass of Yellow stars greater than, less than, or equal to the mass of the Sun?",
    "ai_tutor_available": "false",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "predict_settings": {
      "isPredictLevel": false
    },
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "language": "py",
          "contents": "import pandas as pd\n\nstars = pd.read_csv(\"stars.csv\")\nprint(stars.head())\n\ncolor_groups = stars.groupby(\"Color\")\naverage_mass_by_color = color_groups[\"Mass\"].mean()\n\nred_average_mass = average_mass_by_color.loc[\"Red\"]\n\nprint(\"AVERAGE MASS OF RED STARS:\", red_average_mass)",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true,
          "open": true
        },
        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "stars.csv",
